<title>USA: U.S. brass mill copper stocks lower in Dec - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. brass mill copper stocks lower in Dec - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. brass mill copper stocks fell to 143,800 short tons (copper content) at the end of December from 144,100 short tons in November, said American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>Scrap consumption was 40,000 short tons in the month, down from a November tally of 54,200 short tons.</p>
<p>Refinery shapes consumption was 31,400 short tons in December against 40,400 the previous month. Total brass mill shipments fell to 80,400 short tons from 98,300 short tons in November. Total receipts were 80,000 short tons in December, down from November's 100,500 short tons.</p>
<p>--New York Commodities Desk 212-859-1640</p>
